.TH BIND 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
bind \- assign an address to a socket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int bind(int descriptor, const struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Assigns an address of the specified byte length to a socket.
Unix\-domain and IPv4 address structures are declared in
.B <sys/un.h>
and
.BR <netinet/in.h> .
IPv4 fields must be in network byte order; Crunch does not provide byte\-order
conversion functions.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR socket (3crunch),
.BR bind (2)
